WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.560
INTRO:
Over the past few weeks, we’ve talked about

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:08.069
how California has the highest poverty levels
in the country and how New York is the fastest

00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:10.300
shrinking state in the country.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.750
Considering the dire state of these two regions,
it’s not surprising that a lot of people

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:16.640
are looking for a new home.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:22.190
On TV, we always hear about these people moving
to Texas and Florida, but the fastest growing

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:26.359
state in the US in terms of percentage is
actually Idaho.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:32.480
Between July of 2020 and July of 2021, Idaho’s
population grew by 2.9%.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.510
This is nearly three times higher than the
growth rate of Texas or Florida.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.870
This isn’t some new phenomenon either.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:42.610
Idaho has consistently topped the growth charts
for the past 10 years.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:48.710
Since 2011 Idaho’s population has grown
by over 20% while even Texas’ population

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:50.219
has only grown by 15%.

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:55.989
Now of course, Texas has far greater nominal
growth, but it’s crazy to think that a state

00:00:55.989 --> 00:01:01.329
like Idaho, which is generally overlooked,
is so popular amongst migrants.

00:01:01.329 --> 00:01:05.089
So, why are so many people moving to Idaho?

00:01:05.089 --> 00:01:11.780
COST OF LIVING:
Starting with the most obvious reason, we

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:13.450
have finance.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:17.009
Idaho is simply a far more affordable place
to live than much of the country.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:22.390
Now, Idaho isn’t dirt cheap like Arkansas
or Oklahoma, but they’re definitely on the

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:23.969
reasonable side of things.

00:01:23.969 --> 00:01:26.819
For example, let’s take a look at housing.

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:31.009
Housing prices have actually shot up quite
bit over the past 2 years in Idaho even more

00:01:31.009 --> 00:01:33.119
so than the rest of the country.

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:39.479
Before the pandemic started, the average house
cost $300,000, but now the average house costs

00:01:39.479 --> 00:01:40.659
$475,000.

00:01:40.659 --> 00:01:45.349
This means that Idaho housing has shot up
58% over the past 2 years.

00:01:45.349 --> 00:01:52.039
But if you scroll back to lets say 2016, the
average house cost $211,000 and in 2013, the

00:01:52.039 --> 00:01:54.130
average house cost $154,000.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:58.909
So, as you can see, Idaho has historically
had cheap housing costs.

00:01:58.909 --> 00:02:03.279
And even now, the average house in Idaho is
only slightly more expensive than the national

00:02:03.279 --> 00:02:06.020
average of $440,000.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:11.340
Something else to consider is that the majority
of migrants to Idaho come directly from California.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:16.620
In fact, Californians have made up 46% of
the net migration to Idaho over the past 5

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.620
years.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:21.560
And these guys are not only used to seeing
far more expensive housing prices, but many

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:26.849
of them have also earned California inflated
salaries for several years if not over a decade.

00:02:26.849 --> 00:02:29.290
This is especially true for tech workers.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:33.131
For someone who’s worked at FAANG as a software
engineer throughout their 20s, buying a house

00:02:33.131 --> 00:02:35.819
in Idaho even with cash seems pretty realistic.

00:02:35.819 --> 00:02:38.970
It’s not just housing that’s affordable
either.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:42.769
Every facet of life in Idaho is cheaper than
most of it’s western neighbors.

00:02:42.769 --> 00:02:47.110
In fact, Idaho is the 19th most affordable
place to live in the US.

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:52.090
For perspective, Washington comes in at 38,
Oregon comes in at 47, California comes in

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:53.700
at 49.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:57.859
Considering this, it’s no wonder that Idaho
is a top choice for people living in these

00:02:57.859 --> 00:02:58.859
states.

00:02:58.859 --> 00:03:02.439
It’s not all perfect though, Idaho does
have some hefty taxes.

00:03:02.439 --> 00:03:07.750
In fact, Idaho has one of the highest state
income taxes in the nation coming in at number

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:08.750
6.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:11.760
To make things worse, you don’t even have
to make that much to fall into the highest

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:12.910
tax bracket.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:17.909
As long as you make over $7,940 per year,
you have to pay 6.5%.

00:03:17.909 --> 00:03:21.090
So, this is basically everybody who has a
job.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:26.340
Even in California, you have to make over
$35,000 per year to pay such a tax rate.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:30.330
Idaho also has substantial sales tax as well
coming in at 6%.

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:34.579
For perspective, California’s sales tax
rate is 7.25%.

00:03:34.579 --> 00:03:38.409
On the brightside though, property taxes are
relatively low in Idaho.

00:03:38.409 --> 00:03:43.790
The average resident pays an effective tax
rate of 0.69% which works out to roughly $1,500

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.349
per year.

00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:48.700
This is one of the places that Idaho shines
above even Texas.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:53.040
Texas is notorious for having high property
taxes to make up for a lack of income tax.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:59.440
The average Texan pays an effective property
tax of 1.8% which works out to $3,900 per

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:00.440
year.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:03.700
Also, something else to note is that states
generally have caps as to how much property

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.969
values can increase in a given year.

00:04:05.969 --> 00:04:09.170
For example, the cap in Texas is 10%.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:13.310
This means that even if you’re property
skyrockets in value by 40%, you’d only be

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:15.500
taxed 10% more the following year.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:19.509
So, most of these tax assessments haven’t
caught up to current home prices.

00:04:19.509 --> 00:04:22.900
Once they do, Idaho will likely just become
even more appealing.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:28.350
So, while Idaho has it’s ups and downs financially,
in the big picture, Idaho is far cheaper than

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:32.690
most of the western states that people are
immigrating from.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:37.740
CAREER OPPORTUNITIES:
Aside from offering an affordable life, Idaho

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.780
also offers quite a few career opportunities.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:45.150
You see, it’s not just people that have
moved from western states to Idaho, but also

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:46.150
companies.

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:50.930
Of course, they also benefit from all the
cost savings just like everyone else, but

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:53.090
there’s more to it than just that.

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:57.190
Idaho can sometimes be a more desirable expansion
choice than Texas due to it’s proximity.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:01.710
Here’s the thing, flights between San Francisco
and Boise aren’t even two hours long.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:06.030
Meanwhile, flights between Austin and San
Francisco take nearly 4 hours.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:10.349
Idaho’s proximity to California becomes
an even larger advantage if your other options

00:05:10.349 --> 00:05:12.370
are New York or Florida.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:16.920
It takes over 6 hours to travel from either
of these places to San Francisco.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:20.740
Considering this, as a business, if you need
employees to travel between your offices on

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:25.229
a regular basis, it makes a lot of sense to
choose Idaho and that’s exactly what many

00:05:25.229 --> 00:05:27.070
tech companies have done.

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:31.949
Something else to note is that Idaho’s proximity
makes it a prime destination for remote workers.

00:05:31.949 --> 00:05:35.710
Even before the pandemic, Idaho was one of
the leaders in terms of remote work.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:41.400
In fact, Idaho ranked 6th in the nation with
5.9% of their workforce working remotely.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:45.130
During the pandemic, this number obviously
went to the moon reaching heights of nearly

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:46.300
50%.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:50.699
Since then, companies have been shifting back
to in person, but many employees are choosing

00:05:50.699 --> 00:05:52.289
to stay remote permanently.

00:05:52.289 --> 00:05:56.830
Sometimes this means shifting to another company
that allows for remote work or even negotiating

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.070
a lower salary.

00:05:58.070 --> 00:06:03.129
A Tesla employee named Solomon for example
accepted a 20% pay cut to stay in Idaho.

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:06.930
Stories like these have actually become so
common that companies have started developing

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:09.850
streamlined policies for pay cuts and remote
work.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:14.409
Google for instance is cutting pay by 5 to
25% based on where a remote employee moved

00:06:14.409 --> 00:06:15.409
to.

00:06:15.409 --> 00:06:18.710
It’s not just tech workers that are having
a blast in Idaho either.

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:21.510
Idaho offers plenty of blue collar jobs as
well.

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:24.710
A great example is Idaho’s lumber industry.

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:28.070
Idaho has the 8th highest lumber production
in the nation.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:31.750
And given how much lumber prices have gone
up over the past two years, this has been

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:32.750
quite lucrative.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:37.190
A similar case could be made for Idaho’s
food processing, chemicals, paper, and mining

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:38.990
industries as well.

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:43.669
Idaho ranks 7th when it comes to agricultural
goods and food product exports per capita.

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:49.440
Similarly, 45% of all silver mined in the
US comes from Idaho and Idaho is the second

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:51.560
largest producer of Phosphate.

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:54.340
And this isn’t just cherry picked evidence
either.

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:58.370
There are stats that show that Boise not only
has a strong labor market, but the strongest

00:06:58.370 --> 00:06:59.870
in the entire nation.

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:02.259
Take job posting growth for example.

00:07:02.259 --> 00:07:07.439
Between February of 2020 and Janaury of 2022,
Boise saw the highest growth in job postings

00:07:07.439 --> 00:07:11.810
in the nation coming in at an impressive 94.8%.

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:15.790
In other words, job opportunities literally
doubled in the past two years in Boise.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:20.740
So, there’s no question that Boise is one
of the best places to start a long term career

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.330
right now.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:27.939
CHERRY ON TOP:
The two factors that we’ve discussed so

00:07:27.939 --> 00:07:32.440
far alone are likely enough to convince most
people to at least consider Idaho.

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:36.800
But, there are many more factors that actually
push them to make the decision.

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:40.439
For example, they might be convinced by Idaho’s
beautiful outdoors.

00:07:40.439 --> 00:07:46.240
While Idaho isn’t warm year round like California,
many prefer Idaho because it actually has

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:47.639
4 distinguishable seasons.

00:07:47.639 --> 00:07:52.259
You can experience a full winter, spring,
summer, and fall every year.

00:07:52.259 --> 00:07:56.099
Not to mention, there’s plenty of activities
to do outside thanks to Idaho’s largely

00:07:56.099 --> 00:07:57.540
preserved nature.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:02.180
Idaho has over 2000 named lakes and 4.7 million
acres of designated wilderness.

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:06.939
They also have plenty of mountains which make
the state perfect for hiking, mountain biking,

00:08:06.939 --> 00:08:10.409
skiing, snowboarding, fishing, and so much
more.

00:08:10.409 --> 00:08:13.550
You also don’t have to worry about natural
disasters ruining the landscape either.

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:19.200
Idaho is safe from earthquakes, wildfires,
floods, volcanic eruptions, tsunamis, etc.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:23.650
Aside from the great outdoors, Idaho also
benefits from the perks of suburban life such

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:25.199
as safety and schooling.

00:08:25.199 --> 00:08:27.900
Starting with safety, Idaho has relatively
low crime.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:34.290
On average, there are 227.1 violent crimes
reported for every 100,000 people in the state.

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:38.350
The national average is 380.6 violent crimes
per 100,000 people.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:44.410
Similarly, the states robbery average comes
in 11.4 incidents per 100,000 people which

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:46.420
is the second lowest in the country.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:52.320
These promising statistics carry over to property
crimes as well which come in at 1,461.4 per

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:53.480
100,000.

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:57.630
The national overage is nearly 2,200 per 100,000
people.

00:08:57.630 --> 00:09:01.400
Considering all this, I don’t think you’d
be surprised to hear that Idaho ranks as the

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.810
3rd safest state in the country.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:07.580
In terms of schooling, Idaho’s public school
system is nothing to brag about, but it is

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:08.810
respectable.

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:12.880
It comes in at right about average in the
country at rank 29.

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:16.910
Something to note, however, is that Idaho
ranks better than Texas and Oregon.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:22.100
Also, the only reason California ranks better
than Idaho is due to their higher education.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:26.750
If we look at K-12 education, Idaho comes
in at rank 23 while California comes in at

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:27.750
rank 40.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:32.160
So, if these are your other options, Idaho
is actually relatively good.

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:36.190
Moving on from education, Idaho is great for
proximity to the west coast.

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:40.560
This is not only an advantage for tech companies
located in California but also an advantage

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:42.530
for people with family on the west coast.

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:46.310
A lot of times, the number one reason that
people don’t want to leave a state like

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:49.570
California is because they have a lot friends
and family there.

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:54.190
But, given Idaho’s close proximity to California,
it’s not that expensive or difficult to

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:56.000
visit on a regular basis.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:00.840
This is one of the main reasons that Las Vegas
is so popular amongst Californians as well.

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:05.180
Las Vegas doesn't quite have the same career
opportunities as Boise though, so for many,

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:06.180
Idaho is the best compromise.

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:11.840
THE CASE OF IDAHO:
At the end of the day, over the past few years,

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:16.700
people have been facing economic pressures
from all directions.

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:20.950
We have high inflation, a supply shortage,
skyrocketing home prices, rising interest

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:23.580
rates, and we’re officially in a recession.

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:27.580
With all that being said, people have been
desperate to find a place with a more reasonable

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:30.170
cost of living without having to give up too
much.

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:34.460
For many higher earners like managers and
high level software engineers, the solution

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:36.350
has been moving to Texas and Florida.

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:41.410
But, for many everyday people, they can feel
these states becoming too expensive as well.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:45.740
In Austin, for example, median home prices
are nearly $700,000.

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:51.030
So, many have chosen to move to the next best
thing which seems to be Idaho.

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:54.810
Dozens of secondary tech companies have moved
or expanded to Boise which has made career

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:56.620
opportunities abundant.

00:10:56.620 --> 00:11:01.230
Combine this with a low cost of living, diverse
weather, great outdoors, respectable schooling,

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:06.300
low crime, and close proximity to the west
coast, and it’s no wonder why Idaho has

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:08.020
become so desirable.

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:11.970
The sad part though is that this mass migration
has carried over many of the west coast’s

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:13.850
problems over to Idaho.

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:18.260
For example, Boise suffers from the worst
rush hour traffic in the entire country.

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:21.580
Similarly, home prices are almost crossing
$500,000.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:26.540
So, it’s not clear how much longer Boise
will remain a top choice for new migrants.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:30.330
But, for the people who moved in over the
past 5 years, and especially those that moved

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:34.500
in right before the pandemic, it looks like
they chose the perfect time to make the move,

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.620
but only time will tell.

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:38.420
Would you guys move to Idaho?

